{
  "id": "public-nskips-crossover",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Skip-count signal across planted message lengths",
  "question": "At what tested length does the correct-key skip count of a planted message separate from random ciphertext and key pairs under the source's exact decoder?",
  "reader_question": "How much text is needed before a skip-count clue becomes useful?",
  "summary": "Replays a published ten-length instrument experiment with a planted skip cipher, 300 same-length random pairs per decoder mode and a fixed 1% comparison bar.",
  "finding": "For the exact decoder, the first separating ladder point is 6,000 runes, bracketed by a non-separating 3,600-rune point; separation persists at 9,000 and 12,956. This is a property of the planted test and its chosen null, not an LP2 decryption.",
  "limitations": "Only one English-source plant per length was made. The random ciphertext/key null is not a model of all wrong puzzle keys, the planned shuffle surrogate was not run, and no LP2 keys were screened. The permissive drift channel has a distinct left-tail artifact; the skip-by-two mechanism fails recovery. The labels on the 6,000-rune panel are English windows, not language corpora.",
  "next_steps": "A proposed LP2 skip rule needs an executable generator and decoder, a planted recovery control, a null matching its key search, and a held-out manuscript check. Do not transfer the 6,000-rune crossing to a different rule without measuring it.",
  "outcome": "supported",
  "tags": [
    "key skips",
    "skip count",
    "positive control",
    "null model",
    "window length",
    "source replay"
  ],
  "scope": {
    "pages": [],
    "artifacts": [
      "experiments/records/public-nskips-crossover/source/liber-primus/data/keys/self_reliance.txt"
    ],
    "representation": "Source-planted GP-index ciphertexts of ten lengths from 400 through 12,956 runes, paired with their correct keystream; uniform random GP-index ciphertext and key pairs form each 300-trial null. No unsolved LP2 ciphertext is decoded.",
    "procedure": "First reproduce the L400 and L12956 source gates; then run its ten-length ladder for exact keyskip1 and permissive drift decoders, the separate skip-by-two plant curve, and four additional 6,000-rune English-window labels. Compare correct-key skip counts with exact empirical null tails and require at least 90% planted recovery.",
    "parameters": "Seed 3301; support 0.83; lengths 400, 600, 900, 1,200, 1,600, 2,400, 3,600, 6,000, 9,000, 12,956; 300 null decodes for each of 20 unique length/mode groups; 34 reported cells; empirical two-sided bar 0.01.",
    "exclusions": "Other plaintext windows or distributions, other skip mechanisms or decoder transition rules, a complete key search, LP2 test pages, alternative nulls and the order-preserving shuffle surrogate mentioned in the plan."
  },
